6. How Does Node.js Handle Blocking and Non-Blocking Code Execution?
* Blocking (Synchronous): Blocks the single thread, preventing any other code or requests from running until the operation completes.
* Non-Blocking (Asynchronous): Registers a callback/promise and offloads heavy tasks to Libuv, allowing Node.js to handle other incoming requests immediately.